[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Live-account acceptance for a provider is a two-turn CLI check with a real
authenticated application profile: the first turn returns a fresh random marker,
and a second CLI/native process resumes the same session and recalls it without
the marker in the second prompt. Evidence retains only pass/fail metadata and a
session fingerprint, excluding prompts, responses, credentials and account IDs.
Credentials stay in the application profile and are never uploaded to GitHub.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Antigravity runtime versions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-RUNTIME-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Vetted and discovered version catalog
STATEMENT: >>>
Accounts → Gemini / Antigravity → Runtime management lists existing vetted
versions and versions discovered through **Check for updates**. Gemini /
Antigravity uses GPUI-kit 0.8.0's single-select ``Combobox`` and one review/install
button for the chosen version. Keyboard Up/Down/Enter select a version without
starting installation. Refresh retains an available selection and falls back to
the first release if it disappears; review resolves the refreshed checksum.
The ACP registry's latest platform archive and
SHA-256 are saved atomically to ``<explicit-home>/runtimes/antigravity/releases.json``;
later checks and host restarts retain earlier observed versions. Inspect reads
this catalog offline. This is a known/observed catalog, not an exhaustive upstream
release history. Existing Windows x64 and macOS x64/arm64 support remains.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/runtime_catalog.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/runtimes.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/maintenance.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-RUNTIME-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Compatible runtime release API
STATEMENT: >>>
The additive ``RuntimeInfo.releases`` list uses the existing authenticated runtime
API and application service. ``release`` remains compatible with older clients;
new desktop clients also accept old single-release responses. Web/CLI currently
have no runtime-management UI, and scoped MCP has no install tool. No provider
protocol, account credentials or global developer profiles are changed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/runtime_catalog.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/runtimes.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/maintenance.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-RUNTIME-3
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Release metadata validation and installation
STATEMENT: >>>
Pure metadata validation accepts only version/platform-matching Google URLs and
SHA-256 digests. The existing installer verifies downloads, archives and the native
protocol before atomic activation and preserves previous installation directories.
BDD regressions cover old/new desktop selection and exact install requests,
authenticated HTTP, accumulated catalog/restart, invalid metadata/checksums and
legacy response compatibility. An opt-in (ignored) live integration test installs
the latest and a previous Google release in a temporary home, validating the ACP
runtime and retaining both; it does not log in or run model inference.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/runtime_catalog.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/runtimes.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/maintenance.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
.. code-block:: text

   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-domain --test runtime_catalog
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-infrastructure --test runtimes
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-api --test maintenance
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-desktop --filter given_old_and_new_antigravity_versions
   cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent-infrastructure --test runtimes given_live_google_releases -- --ignored --nocapture

Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/agentclientprotocol/registry/main/antigravity-acp/agent.json

Native visual acceptance covers the listed versions, old/new review URLs and
checksums, and cancellation without installation.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Common MCP registration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-MCP-REGISTRY-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Shared MCP catalog for all providers
STATEMENT: >>>
Settings → Plugins → MCP registers standalone servers once for Claude, Codex and
Antigravity. The shared catalog is ``mcp.json`` in the explicit application home;
``GET/PUT /v1/mcp`` is the provider-independent endpoint. Existing
``/v1/mcp/{provider}`` routes remain compatible aliases. Server composition,
desktop, web and CLI use the same common catalog. A native Config without
``mcp_home`` retains its standalone-profile behavior for adapter consumers.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/http.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/agent/tests/protocols.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/mcp.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-MCP-REGISTRY-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Legacy profile deduplication and preservation
STATEMENT: >>>
Before the first shared save, identical legacy definitions across default and
named account profiles are deduplicated in memory. Conflicting names require
review of the original profile files; reading never rewrites them. A shared
save, including ``[]``, becomes authoritative and preserves original profile files
and OAuth credentials. OAuth remains scoped by provider/account; its account
selector appears only when OAuth authentication needs management.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/http.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/agent/tests/protocols.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/mcp.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-MCP-REGISTRY-3
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Registration does not select tools
STATEMENT: >>>
Registration does not select tools. The desktop conversation-header checkboxes
still control optional MCP per turn, and new conversations start empty. Saving
refreshes the checkbox catalog without changing existing choices. A common
update is rejected while any provider has pending jobs or an active profile
operation. Enabled plugin names are checked across all available registered
workspaces while holding the same catalog lock as plugin activation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/http.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/agent/tests/protocols.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/mcp.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Authenticated HTTP tests cover common/compatibility routes, three-provider
visibility, legacy conflicts and preservation, invalid-update rollback, empty
saves and scoped OAuth. Native process fixtures pass one shared file to all
three provider adapters and cover selected/empty/omitted choices without writes.
Repository regressions reproduce cross-workspace plugin collisions and catalog
lock contention. Rendered desktop tests cover common registration and OAuth
target switching without discarding the common editor.

Native fixture visual acceptance covers registration without provider tabs,
all-provider authenticated reads, checkbox selection, updated catalogs preserving
existing choices, and new-chat reset, without live provider inference or a real
remote MCP service.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Conversation extension quick check

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-EXTENSIONS-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unified plugin picker per conversation
STATEMENT: >>>
The desktop header has one **Connect plugins / 플러그인 연결** picker for installed
plugins, skills and configured MCP servers. Search and type filters narrow the
checkbox list. Only checked entries appear in the header with their type icon and
name. Unchecking affects subsequent turns of this conversation, preserving global
plugin/skill enablement, MCP configuration and OAuth state. New chats start empty;
drafts and saved guidance receipts retain the original conversation's choices.
Editing only package/MCP choices also permits a revised question to be submitted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/conversation_extensions.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/agent/tests/protocols.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests/conversation_context.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-EXTENSIONS-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Optional extensions contract
STATEMENT: >>>
The optional chat/revision ``extensions`` contract is applied in the application
Guidance path and shared native Config filter. Omitted selection preserves
existing web/CLI/HTTP/MCP callers. Explicit empty selection suppresses optional
MCP and unselected skill discovery while retaining host tools and approvals.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/conversation_extensions.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/agent/tests/protocols.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests/conversation_context.rs

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Rendered desktop tests guard against a separate Skills button, dropped new-chat
draft choices and disabled extension-only revisions. Domain tests cover
validation, empty/omitted distinction and revisions; infrastructure tests
exercise real temporary plugin/guidance files, and history tests reopen/fork the
existing selection receipt. Native protocol selection tests cover all three
providers without real credentials or remote inference.

Native fixture acceptance checks the unified picker, selected header icons/names,
direct checkbox removal, unchanged installed plugin/MCP state via authenticated
reads, and new-chat reset. This is fixture visual acceptance, not live provider
acceptance.

.. code-block:: text

   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-domain --test conversation_extensions
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-desktop
   cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent --test protocols -- --selection-only
   cargo harness check --include-desktop
<<<

