[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Desktop right-side panels

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-PANELS-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stacked work and reference panels
STATEMENT: >>>
Work activity and reference conversations share a resizable right column. When
both are open, work is above the reference with a draggable horizontal divider.
Their toolbar buttons and close buttons operate independently; closing one gives
the remaining panel the whole column. Each panel has its own scroll position.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/presentation/tests/panels.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-PANELS-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Persisted panel layout
STATEMENT: >>>
Dragging the column's left edge changes its shared width. Double-clicking that
edge restores 320 px; double-clicking the horizontal divider restores an equal
split. Width, split ratio, and both visibility preferences are saved in the
desktop home's ``ui-right-panels.json``. Saved widths from ``ui-reference-width``
are used when no new layout is available. Invalid dimensions fall back to safe
defaults. Window constraints preserve a 480 px chat at desktop widths without
overwriting the preferred width; reopening a panel restores the split ratio.
The reference stack keeps the existing focused view at narrow widths, while
work alone appears below chat. The selected reference conversation is not part
of the saved layout.
<<<
