[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Project Git review

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-GIT-REVIEW-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Git as a project tool
STATEMENT: >>>
Git is a project/worktree tool beside the desktop conversation, rather than a
settings menu. The toolbar opens changed files, per-file staged/unstaged diffs,
checkpoints and the existing PR flow. At the default desktop width, chat and Git
remain visible together; narrow windows use the existing focused tool view.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/desktop/src/tests/project_git.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/project_tools.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: apps/web/test.cjs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-GIT-REVIEW-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reviewed commit proposals
STATEMENT: >>>
Scoped agents can call ``workspace_propose_commit`` without general host write
authority. A proposal persists a message, exact paths and the reviewed
branch/HEAD/index/worktree version; it neither stages nor commits. Desktop and
web show a review notice. Operators can edit the message and select files before
explicitly approving. Approval rejects stale versions and preserves unrelated
staging, including intent-to-add files. Renames include source removal without
committing unrelated files recreated at the old path. A commit is published to
the reviewed branch with an expected-parent comparison.
<<<
