   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-api --test project_tools
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-infrastructure
   node --test apps/web/test.cjs
   cargo harness check --include-desktop

Protocol fixtures and temporary Git repositories validate the proposal and
operator execution boundaries without live provider inference.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Required checks for ordinary chat jobs

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
In desktop project settings or the web client's **프로젝트 필수 검증** section,
save the project's required commands as JSON argv arrays, for example:

.. code-block:: json

   [["cargo", "harness", "test", "--package", "gpui-agent-domain"], ["cargo", "harness", "fmt"]]
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-VERIFICATION-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Required command configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
Each command runs directly in the job's workspace, without an implicit shell.
Use an explicit shell executable when a project requires shell syntax. The
operator-only ``PUT /v1/projects/{id}/verification`` accepts up to 8 ``commands``,
``max_attempts`` (default 3, maximum 10), and ``timeout_seconds`` per command
(default 300, maximum 3600). An empty command list disables required checks.
The UI preserves existing attempt and timeout settings when saving commands.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/presentation/tests/tool_activity.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-VERIFICATION-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Repair loop gates completion
STATEMENT: >>>
Given a configured project, when an ordinary durable chat job's provider finishes,
the host runs every required command. A failure starts a repair turn in the same
conversation and reruns every command. Only zero exit codes for all commands and
unchanged source fingerprints permit the job's completed event. Exhaustion,
timeout, missing executables, fingerprint errors, and cancellation cannot produce
a successful completion. The plan is captured at job start; changing settings
does not weaken an already running job's checks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/presentation/tests/tool_activity.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-VERIFICATION-3
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Verification receipts and source fingerprints
STATEMENT: >>>
The activity panel retains each attempt, command, exit code, bounded stdout/stderr,
Git HEAD (when present), and a SHA-256 fingerprint of source paths and contents.
Git projects include tracked and untracked nonignored files, so uncommitted
changes are represented. Plain folders include regular files except host state.
Generated files should be ignored in Git. External links, unsupported non-file
entries, and source sets above the fingerprint limits fail closed. Receipts
survive history reload; interrupted jobs are not silently marked completed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/domain/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/project_verification.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/presentation/tests/tool_activity.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-VERIFICATION-4
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Durable submission paths
STATEMENT: >>>
Desktop, web, and scoped MCP submissions use the durable Jobs service. The legacy
HTTP ``POST /v1/providers/{provider}/chat`` endpoint rejects configured projects
and directs callers to ``/v1/providers/{provider}/jobs``. Standalone CLI ``ask``
retains its existing direct execution path. Registered commands determine
coverage; a zero exit code alone does not establish that a project has meaningful tests.
<<<
