- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/mcp_sessions.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/mcp_sessions.rs

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: MCP tools

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-MCP-TOOLS-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Tool catalog and access levels
STATEMENT: >>>
.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1

   * - Tool
     - Access
     - Result
   * - list_jobs
     - Read
     - Durable environment jobs
   * - get_job
     - Read
     - Original request and current job state
   * - get_job_events
     - Read
     - Persisted events after a sequence cursor
   * - enqueue_job
     - Write
     - Accepted durable job, not a completed provider turn
   * - cancel_job
     - Write
     - Cancellation requested; observe events for completion
   * - conversation_list
     - Read
     - Live offset pages of saved conversations, with durable execution state
   * - conversation_search
     - Read
     - Literal title/content search and bounded matching-message previews
   * - conversation_read
     - Read
     - Unicode-safe message pages without native session IDs or attachment bytes
   * - conversation_rename
     - Write
     - Rename through existing history validation and active-turn checks
   * - conversation_organize
     - Write
     - Set/clear pinned and archived state; omitted fields are preserved
   * - conversation_send
     - Write
     - Idempotent durable message delivery, or new conversation when id is omitted
   * - conversation_wait
     - Read
     - Wait for a selected durable run without cancelling it on timeout
   * - conversation_interrupt
     - Write
     - Interrupt a running/waiting or selected queued run; preserve terminal results
   * - conversation_fork
     - Write
     - Idle branch through a completed assistant boundary, with an independent native session
   * - conversation_merge_back
     - Write
     - Persist branch-only context for an ancestor's next admitted turn
   * - conversation_transfers
     - Read
     - Cursor pages of durable transfer metadata and pending/attached state
   * - attachment_upload
     - Write
     - Validated scoped upload, metadata receipt and identical-content ID reuse
   * - attachment_from_workspace
     - Write
     - Scoped text/line-range or image snapshot; returns metadata without bytes
   * - attachment_list
     - Read
     - At most 16 scoped upload metadata records; no content or source paths
   * - attachment_delete
     - Write
     - Delete staging bytes; accepted job/history copies and retries remain valid
   * - get_pending_questions
     - Read
     - Current live native questions, choices and one-time request ID
   * - answer_questions
     - Operator write
     - Relay user answers or skip; never tool approval
   * - browser_open
     - Write
     - Owned isolated Chromium page and initial bounded DOM snapshot
   * - browser_render_html
     - Write
     - Self-contained HTML in a fresh offline sandbox; returns its DOM snapshot
   * - browser_diagnostics
     - Read
     - Recent console, JavaScript errors and browser logs; bounded, non-destructive sample
   * - browser_snapshot
     - Read
     - Fresh visible text/interactive targets with a new revision
   * - browser_act
     - Write
     - Referenced click/fill or current-page key/scroll, then a fresh snapshot
   * - browser_wait
     - Read
     - Literal body-text condition and matched/timeout result
   * - browser_capture
     - Read
     - Native MCP image block with URL and viewport metadata
   * - browser_close
     - Write
     - Cancel commands and discard only this scope's profile
   * - project_list
     - Read
     - Full operator catalog or only the calling agent's workspace
   * - project_register
     - Operator write
     - Open an existing absolute folder; restore hidden project IDs/history
   * - project_forget
     - Operator write
     - Hide a project without deleting files or history; reject busy workspaces
   * - worktree_create
     - Operator write
     - New branch/worktree in app-owned storage; never overwrite existing branches
   * - worktree_remove
     - Operator write
     - Delete a clean, idle, app-managed worktree; retain branch/history
   * - workspace_changes
     - Read
     - Scoped branch and changed files with index/worktree status
   * - workspace_diff
     - Read
     - Scoped exact-path staged/unstaged diff with truncation flags
   * - workspace_propose_commit
     - Write
     - Pending commit proposal for operator review; read-only scoped sessions may call it; never stages or commits
   * - environment_read
     - Read
     - Stable environment ID, version, OS/architecture and selected preferences
   * - environment_preferences_update
     - Operator write
     - Patch display label and default worktree base
   * - host_skills_list
     - Read
     - Enabled host-managed skill metadata for the session workspace
   * - host_skills_read
     - Read
     - One enabled skill's SKILL.md or supporting UTF-8 resource
   * - host_skill_propose
     - Write
     - Pending skill proposal; installs nothing until the operator approves
   * - host_skill_proposal_status
     - Read
     - Skill proposal state
   * - host_mcp_propose
     - Write
     - Pending workspace MCP server proposal; starts nothing until approval
   * - host_mcp_proposal_status
     - Read
     - MCP server proposal state
   * - write_pull_request_guides
     - Write
     - Queue reviewer-guide jobs for 1–20 GitHub PRs; never posts to GitHub
   * - read_pull_request_guide
     - Read
     - Latest local guide result and head/base staleness
   * - link_pull_request
     - Write
     - Idempotent local PR link for a saved conversation
   * - watch_pull_request
     - Write
     - Poll an open PR and queue turns for new checks, reviews or conflicts
   * - unwatch_pull_request
     - Write
     - Stop a watch, keeping the link
   * - unlink_pull_request
     - Write
     - Remove the local link and its watch
   * - list_thread_pull_requests
     - Read
     - A conversation's local PR links; does not contact GitHub
   * - device_list
     - Read
     - Operator-granted Android devices through the local ADB server
   * - device_open
     - Write
     - Claim a granted, already connected Android device
   * - device_screenshot
     - Read
     - PNG screen image with dimensions and a new revision
   * - device_act
     - Write
     - One tap/swipe/text/key action against the latest revision
   * - device_close
     - Write
     - Release only this scope's device session and grant
   * - computer_capture
     - Read
     - Windows desktop image, dimensions and a new revision
   * - computer_act
     - Write
     - One click/text/key/scroll against the latest revision, then a fresh capture
   * - computer_close
     - Write
     - Release this execution's computer control
<<<
