[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Project tools

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-PROJECT-TOOLS-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Workspace scope for project tools
STATEMENT: >>>
Project tools use Workspaces even when Jobs is absent. Directory management is
hidden from scoped sessions and rejected on direct invocation, including sessions
with write access. Scoped reads default to the session's physical workspace and
cannot select a sibling worktree. Operator reads default to the catalog's default
workspace. No tool changes another session's scope. Creation returns the updated
catalog; find the new workspace by its unique branch. After uncertain delivery,
inspect the catalog before retrying creation/removal: existing branches and
missing workspace IDs return errors. Force removal is not supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/project_tools.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-PROJECT-TOOLS-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Shared mutation guards
STATEMENT: >>>
HTTP and MCP share application-level pending-job checks under the workspace
mutation lease, plus adapter guards for active operations, dirty/ignored files,
locked/main/external worktrees and managed-directory containment. Changes/diff
also reject a registered directory redirected through a symlink or junction.
``cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-api --test project_tools`` covers these
public MCP/HTTP behaviors with temporary real Git repositories, scoped credentials
and a durable queued job; no provider login or live inference is required.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/project_tools.rs

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Browser tools

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-BROWSER-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Isolated browser scopes
STATEMENT: >>>
Browser tools require a HostControl backend, not Jobs or provider login. The
application use case validates commands and image replies; the control adapter
owns isolated browser processes and serializes commands within each scope.
MCP scopes are injected from authentication, never selectable in arguments.
Provider/account/workspace namespaces share no profile with each other, the
operator namespace, manual controls or personal browser profiles. Same-scope
sessions share a single automation page across native turns. The public client
fixture's NoControls backend keeps automation disabled.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/control.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/control/tests/browser_automation.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-BROWSER-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded DOM snapshots and revisions
STATEMENT: >>>
DOM snapshots use a fixed script in a CDP isolated world, with at most 16,000
Unicode characters and 100 interactive targets (viewport targets first), plus
truncation flags. Input values are omitted from target metadata. A string
revision changes on every snapshot, including after actions/waits; click/fill
must use a target ID from that revision. Detached, hidden, covered, inert,
disabled, read-only and unsupported input targets are rejected without losing
the page. Fill replaces a supported input/textarea value and emits input/change
events; user text is JSON encoded as data. Arbitrary script execution is not
exposed. Key/scroll reuse existing bounded controls. Frames, shadow roots,
popups and uploads are outside this interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/control.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/control/tests/browser_automation.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-BROWSER-3
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Waits, capture and profile lifecycle
STATEMENT: >>>
Text waits accept timeout_ms 0–10000 and return matched=false on ordinary
absence while retaining the page. Capture emits an image content block and
keeps base64 out of structured metadata. The adapter caps automation contexts
at eight, reaps profiles idle for ten minutes on a 30-second sweep, and closes
them on protocol failure, a 15-second command limit, request drop, explicit
close or host shutdown. Profiles are temporary and downloads remain blocked.
Actions are not durable/idempotent; observe state before retrying uncertain
delivery. Close is safe to repeat. Closed/reopened pages reject old revisions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/control.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/control/tests/browser_automation.rs

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The authenticated control fixture covers discovery/calls without Jobs,
scope injection, read-only access, invalid input and native image responses.
Explicitly run browser_automation with --ignored for the public-port tests
against a locally installed Chromium and a local HTML server. They cover
Unicode/quote input, DOM clicks, rejected targets/revisions/URLs, text waits,
capture, three scope dimensions, manual/operator isolation, profile reset,
truncation and cancellation while navigation is pending. These tests use no
real accounts. Existing manual browser acceptance remains separately available;
Windows pointer tests are not part of browser automation verification.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-BROWSER-4
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sandboxed HTML rendering
STATEMENT: >>>
HTML results reuse HostControl and the scope's existing browser lifecycle; no
new service, dependency, persistent artifact store or UI panel is required.
Contracts validate a nonempty, NUL-free, 512 KiB UTF-8 source and construct the
escaped srcdoc wrapper. The control adapter owns the fresh process/profile,
inherited CSP, sandbox without same-origin/popups/forms/downloads, blocked
requests, non-forwarding loopback proxy (including implicit loopback bypass
removal), DNS restriction and cross-process iframe CDP session. Inline scripts
and CSS/data assets work; remote/relative assets and module imports do not.
Rendering or switching back to a URL replaces the profile and invalidates targets.
<<<
