[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Conversation tools

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Conversation scope resolution
STATEMENT: >>>
Conversation tools require ``provider``. Omitted ``account``/``workspace`` resolve to
the calling session; sessions cannot select a different scope. Operator tokens
can select registered accounts/workspaces explicitly. Conversation IDs are local
to that scope, while returned job IDs identify durable runs. Reads require no
installed/authenticated provider; message execution uses the existing runtime
and approval policy. Tools are exposed by the shared server/embedded-desktop MCP
adapter and reach all three provider bridges without client-specific protocols.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Queue ordering and submission receipts
STATEMENT: >>>
Queued jobs run in submission order; one worker serializes a provider/account
across all workspaces. Queued jobs cannot be edited or reordered; ``cancel_job``
cancels queued or running work. Submission receipts retain the original
request's fingerprint; identical retries return the same job, while changed
input under the original command ID is rejected.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-3
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pending question relay
STATEMENT: >>>
``get_pending_questions`` requires job ``id`` and returns ``job_id`` and ``pending``
(operation/request IDs, questions, options and multi_select), or ``null`` when
there is no live question. It reads the active application interaction registry
rather than replaying old journal entries, and never consumes a question.
Permission requests are excluded. ``answer_questions`` is listed/callable only
with a writable operator credential: scoped agents cannot supply the user's
answer. Provide the same ``id``, exact ``request_id``, and ``response`` as either
``{"type":"answers","answers":{"question-id":["answer"]}}`` or
``{"type":"cancelled"}`` to skip. Every requested question must be answered;
single-choice questions accept one value, multi-select at most 32, each nonblank
and at most 16 KiB. Existing free-text answers remain valid even with choices.
Invalid answers leave the question pending. Stale/duplicate replies fail and
concurrent replies consume the request only once. Acceptance is delivery to
the runtime, not completion; inspect job state/events. Skipping a question does
not cancel the job, and this tool cannot approve or deny tool permissions.
Cancelling/ending a job clears live questions; interrupted questions are not
replayed after host recovery. Native question support remains Claude/Codex;
Antigravity retains its existing advertised capabilities.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
These tools share application services in the server and embedded desktop MCP
hosts and their native provider bridges. Existing HTTP/web/desktop question
responses retain their contracts; the direct CLI is unchanged. The jobs fixture
tests MCP authorization, queue execution order, Claude/Codex answers/skip,
invalid/concurrent responses and cancellation. The repository fixture verifies
queue scope filtering, paging, restart and original submission receipts.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-4
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Conversation paging
STATEMENT: >>>
List/search pages accept ``offset``, ``limit`` (1–50, default 20), and ``archived``
(``active``, ``archived``, ``all``). Echo ``next_offset``; concurrent updates can change
ordering. Search requires a nonblank ``query`` of at most 256 characters and uses
the existing SQLite literal substring behavior. Message pages accept ``cursor``
and ``limit`` (1–20, default 20) with a shared 16,000-character budget. Echo
``next_cursor`` to recover long messages; ``text`` counts Unicode scalar values,
not bytes or UTF-16 units. Attachments are reported as a count; use existing job
events for activity. These tools page existing in-memory history snapshots.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-5
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Send, wait and interrupt
STATEMENT: >>>
``conversation_send`` requires ``text`` and ``command_id``; optional ``id`` continues
a saved conversation, otherwise a new one is created when its job starts.
Optional ``model`` selects this turn's model; omission uses the provider default,
except the first independent fork turn inherits its saved model.
It shares durable receipts with job submission and queues behind active work.
It does not steer or restart a native turn. ``conversation_wait`` selects the
latest job once at call time unless ``job_id`` is supplied, accepts ``timeout_ms``
of 0–10000 (default 1000), and returns ``timed_out`` plus current job state.
Timeout leaves work running. ``conversation_interrupt`` prefers running/waiting
work over a newer queued message; explicit ``job_id`` targets one run. It does not
cancel other queued messages. Repeating interruption of a terminal job preserves
its result. Both tools validate that a supplied job belongs to the conversation
and scope. They track durable jobs only, not standalone CLI or direct streaming
turns. Renaming an active response is rejected; archiving does not cancel work,
and a later delivered message can unarchive it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-6
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Conversation fork
STATEMENT: >>>
``conversation_fork`` requires source ``id`` and ``command_id``; optional
``through_message_id`` selects a completed assistant boundary (default: current
last message). An earlier completed prefix can be forked while the source is
active. The idle child copies messages, attachments, tool results and model;
native session IDs and approvals are excluded. Pass the returned ``target_id``
as ``conversation_send.id`` to start an independent native session. Optional
``title`` names the child. No provider process starts during the fork.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-7
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Conversation merge-back
STATEMENT: >>>
``conversation_merge_back`` requires ``source_id``, ancestor ``target_id`` and
``command_id``, with an optional completed ``through_message_id``. Only content
after that ancestor's original fork boundary is included, also for nested
branches. Sibling, unrelated, reverse and cross-scope merges are rejected.
The snapshot is saved for the target's next admitted turn; it does not rewrite
messages, start a turn or steer an active provider. This transfers conversation
context, not Git changes. Each snapshot has a 192 KiB transcript limit plus
existing attachment limits. Combined pending context is validated at acceptance
and again with caller attachments at turn admission. Rejection leaves history
and pending records unchanged.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/history/tests/context_transfers.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONVERSATION-8
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Atomic fork and merge receipts
STATEMENT: >>>
Fork/merge commands and their receipts commit atomically in history. Identical
retries return the same record even after source updates/deletion or restart;
changed input with the same command ID is rejected. Receipts and snapshots live
until the target is deleted. ``conversation_transfers`` requires ``id`` and accepts
an ``after`` transfer ID (default 0), returning at most 50 metadata records and
``next_after``. Snapshot bytes and native session IDs are excluded. ``pending``
means saved intent; ``attached`` means committed into an admitted user turn, not
provider completion. Merge context remains in that turn's saved attachments and
is not attached again to later turns. The repository BDD scenarios cover all
three providers, source deletion/restart, nested deltas, admission rollback and
tool-result preservation without permission inheritance; the MCP jobs fixture
covers authorization, concurrent retries, model inheritance and delivery.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
