[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Durable intent

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-DURABILITY-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Idempotent job submission
STATEMENT: >>>
``enqueue_job`` requires a ``command_id``. REST clients opt into the same application
service with ``Idempotency-Key`` on job submission. A receipt and its job commit in
one SQLite transaction. Concurrent identical retries return the original job;
different input or scope with the same ID is rejected. Receipts retain only a
SHA-256 fingerprint of the original scope/request and live as long as their job.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-DURABILITY-2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Durable queue as execution outbox
STATEMENT: >>>
The existing durable queue is the execution outbox: work is saved before a worker
is woken, startup wakes queued jobs, and running/waiting jobs become interrupted
after a host crash. Interrupted provider work is never automatically replayed,
because the external process may already have changed files. Existing context
snapshot and checkpoint services keep this lifecycle.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-DURABILITY-3
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Correlated MCP diagnostics
STATEMENT: >>>
MCP emits one structured stderr record per executed tool, containing its registered
name, success flag, elapsed milliseconds, and host-generated ``request_id``. The
HTTP response carries the same value in ``X-Request-ID``; client-supplied identifiers
are not copied into diagnostics. Successful job reads, submissions and cancellation
also include ``job_id`` and the current ``operation_id`` when execution has started.
Retries have distinct request IDs and share a durable job ID. IDs are process-scoped;
the job ID and persisted event sequence connect later reads to execution state.
Arguments, tokens, account/workspace paths and returned content are excluded.
``McpDiagnostic`` is pure data; ``McpDiagnosticSink`` is an output port. The HTTP adapter
supplies the default stderr output or an injected sink without coupling use cases
to a logging backend.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/infrastructure/tests/queue.rs

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Windows computer use MVP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-COMPUTER-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Automatic host computer policy
STATEMENT: >>>
Production Windows desktop and server hosts automatically enable computer use
and manual desktop control for every project for the lifetime of the host.
No monitor-panel grant or ten-minute renewal is required. Authority is never
saved to disk. Each new host starts with this policy enabled; shutdown clears
the in-memory control state. A separately running server owns its own lifetime.
<<<
