UID: HARNESS-COMPUTER-7
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Opt-in live runner and ACP tool identity
STATEMENT: >>>
This opt-in runner never invokes personal desktop I/O and does not run in the
default test suite. It fails on an unresolved native interaction, missing
computer actions, failure/cancellation, or a 200-second deadline; host teardown
still cancels unfinished work. Antigravity uses the native
``localharness_external`` executable beside its ACP server. ACP supplies
authoritative tool identity in ``toolCall._meta.mcp.server/tool``; the policy uses
that metadata, not display titles or input arguments. Positive and negative
domain cases and a native ACP-process fixture cover this boundary. Native
fixtures remain separate from the real-model and physical Windows tests.
