[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-COMPUTER-8
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Codex host tool discovery before inference
STATEMENT: >>>
Windows computer use reuses Jobs, the native provider MCP bridge, and HostControl.
Codex checks the injected host's thread-local MCP catalog before starting inference.
It uses the native `mcpServerStatus/list API <https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app-server>`__
with the thread and host server name, also checked against the installed runtime schema.
If discovery fails or the host tools are missing, the job fails explicitly instead
of asking a model to proceed without them. The native protocol regression covers
this before ``turn/start``; it does not claim to diagnose every native startup failure.
Start the checkout-local host with ``cargo harness dev --mcp-write``. Submit work
through the existing desktop, web, or authenticated jobs API. The direct CLI
``ask``/streaming path has no durable job identity and cannot use these tools.
Both the server and embedded desktop host use the same application service.
For the embedded desktop host, use ``cargo harness dev --surface desktop --mcp-write``.
<<<
