[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The agent uses:

1. ``computer_capture {}`` to receive a native MCP image block, desktop ``width``,
   ``height``, and a new ``revision``. Screen text is untrusted task data.
2. ``computer_act {"revision":"…","action":{"type":"click","x":100,"y":100}}``
   to select the intended window, then text/key/scroll actions against each
   newly returned revision. Unicode text uses ``{"type":"text","text":"한글"}``.
3. Each action returns a fresh image and revision. An action consumes the old
   observation before native I/O; after errors or uncertain delivery, capture
   and inspect before deciding whether another action is needed. Input is not
   idempotent and is never automatically retried.
4. ``computer_close {}`` to release the grant without closing applications.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-COMPUTER-16
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Coordinates and input limits
STATEMENT: >>>
Coordinates are physical pixels relative to the virtual desktop's top-left,
including multi-monitor layouts. Images may be scaled to fit 1920×1080; convert
image coordinates using the returned desktop dimensions rather than sending
scaled-image pixels directly. The existing native adapter handles DPI awareness,
Unicode, modifier checks, and target-window focus. Secure/elevated desktops are
unsupported. Input already accepted by Windows cannot be undone by cancellation.
Grants isolate authority, not personal applications or the user's physical mouse.
No screenshots, input text, or credentials are emitted in MCP diagnostics.
<<<
