[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Headless acceptance uses real HTTP/MCP, SQLite Jobs, all three native provider
fixtures, and a substituted native desktop driver (the real grant/revision policy
stays in place):

.. code-block:: text

   cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent-api --test jobs -- --computer-only
   cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent-api --test jobs -- --mcp-sessions-only
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-control
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent-application --test architecture

Actual Windows capture/click/Unicode input/re-observation uses an owned EDIT
test window and briefly moves the pointer. It needs an unlocked interactive
Windows desktop, no provider login:

.. code-block:: text

   cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent-control --lib live_windows_capture_and_input -- --ignored --nocapture

Optionally set ``GPUI_AGENT_QA_DIR`` to an absolute directory outside the checkout
to retain ``windows-computer-mvp.jpg``. This is visual/native verification, separate
from fixture acceptance and from live model inference. Accessibility tree
navigation, drag/chords, and macOS/Linux desktop drivers are outside this MVP.

For inline grant UI visual acceptance without real provider accounts or host
controls, run ``cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent-api --test jobs -- --computer-fixture``
in a retained interactive terminal. Connect the desktop with the printed loopback
URL and fixture-only token file. This reuses SQLite Jobs and the native provider
fixtures, plus the real computer grant policy with a synthetic desktop driver;
browser/device/manual desktop effects remain disabled. It starts one waiting job.
Exercise inline confirmation cancellation, approve/revoke, job-history cancellation,
refresh and narrow-window scrolling; retain screenshots outside the checkout. Close the
owned client and press Enter in the fixture terminal; its supervisor removes the
temporary home after the host exits. This is a visual fixture run, not live model
inference or actual OS input.
<<<

