[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-LIVE-EDITOR-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Negative live scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor mode creates the same owned Win32 EDIT window but injects no input.
For revoke/cancel/decline acceptance, additionally set
``GPUI_AGENT_QA_EDITOR_EMPTY=1``. The final Enter then asserts the editor is still
empty. Keep it open across the three negative scenarios and inspect it after
each. Stop at a native text approval: revoke and decline it in the first job,
cancel the second job from that dialog, and decline the third request. Confirm
terminal results and no granted owner after the model closes or the job ends.
All operator mutations must use desktop controls. Independent HTTP GETs may
verify terminal journals; they must not submit approvals or change grants.
Stop the live host and owned editor before ``cargo harness check --include-desktop``:
the harness fixture gate rebuilds the same test executables, which Windows locks
while they are running.
The live Jobs runner references the explicit profile without copying credentials,
uses temporary SQLite/project state and a fresh operator token, and enables only
the default Codex account. It never initiates login/logout. Connect the built
desktop with an explicit checkout-local ``--home``, the printed ``--api-url``, and
``--token-file``. Submit a Codex job using ``on-request`` and ``read-only``; restrict
the instruction to the three computer tools and the owned blank editor.
<<<
