[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Profile contention before approval

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
.. code-block:: text

   cargo test --locked -p gpui-agent-api --test jobs -- --profile-contention-only
   cargo harness test --package gpui-agent --test profile_contention
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HARNESS-CONTENTION-1
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Prompt waits for the profile lock
STATEMENT: >>>
A status read and a starting prompt share the native profile lock. Previously,
the prompt failed immediately on contention, closing the job stream before an
approval (``Missing interaction``). The HTTP/native fixture holds the status read
with readiness/release signals to reproduce that ordering. It verifies observable
waiting, approval after release, cancellation while waiting, and repeated status
polling on all three providers. The native adapter test checks that the prompt's
deadline includes lock acquisition and that waiting emits one notice. These use
synthetic profiles and processes, and the API cases also run in the full jobs suite.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/api/tests/jobs.rs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: crates/agent/tests/profile_contention.rs

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
